 34S  c  Nuclear resonance fluorescence (NRF) measurements:                     
 34S  c  1984Be26: {+34}S(pol |g,|g') with 18-MeV unpolarized and linearly      
 34S 2c  polarized bremsstrahlung beams from the 65-MeV electron linac at the   
 34S 3c  University of Giessen. Targets were mixtures of of H3BO3, C, MgO, Si,  
 34S 4c  and S. |g rays were detected using four Ge(Li) detectors atazimuthal   
 34S 5c  angles of 0|', 90|', 180|', and 270|' relative to the polarization     
 34S 6c  plane of the linearly polarized beam. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced       
 34S 7c  levels, J, decay widths to the ground state (|G{-0}), and              
 34S 8c  electric/magnetic characters from azimuthal asymmetry of scattered |g  
 34S 9c  rays.                                                                  
 34S  c  1978Be46: {+34}S(|g,|g') with an 18-MeV electron bremsstrahlung beam   
 34S 2c  from the 65-MeV electron linac at the University of Giessen on a 1-g   
 34S 3c  self-supporting 77.9%-enriched {+34}S target. |g rays were detected    
 34S 4c  using a Ge(Li) detector at 125|' relative to the bremsstrahlung beam.  
 34S 5c  Measured E|g, I|g, and integrated (|g,|g') scattering cross sections.  
 34S 6c  Deduced levels, J, and decay widths to the ground state (|G{-0}). Aslo 
 34S 7c  see 1977BeYD.                                                          
 34S  cG E$From level energy differences.                                       
 34S  cL J$Based on the general statement that nuclear resonance fluorescence   
 34S 2cL populates mostly J=1 states and to a lesser extent J=2+ states, whence 
 34S 3cL the tentative spin assignments (by evaluators). Parity determined by   
 34S 4cL the (pol |g,|g') experiment (1984Be26) is firmly adopted               
 34S  cL T$Assuming J=1 and 100% decay to g.s.                                  
